[Name] Steam
[Summary] Valve's Steam gaming platform.
[License] Proprietary
[Description] Steam for Linux, the client for Valve's digital distribution platform. Ships the official launcher plus the 32-bit client bootstrap (bootstraplinux_ubuntu12_32.tar.xz). The client is 32-bit, so a 32-bit base (Glibc-32) and 32-bit GPU driver libraries are required. On first run Steam downloads its scout runtime into ~/.local/share/Steam; for an offline Live CD bake the runtime into the squashfs image first.
[Homepage] https://store.steampowered.com
